## Inversion, and the well-formedness of the rules

// A judgement form is MEANINGFUL only when its presuppositions hold
// (the displays above): a derivation of Γ ⊦ a₀ ≐ a₁ : A takes Γ ctx,
// Γ ⊦ A type, Γ ⊦ a₀ : A and Γ ⊦ a₁ : A for granted, and a rule is
// applicable only where its conclusion is meaningful. So nothing about
// derivations needs proving to KNOW that a derivable judgement has
// well-formed parts: that is what the form says. A RULE IS WELL-FORMED
// when its premises, with their own presuppositions, yield the
// presuppositions of its conclusion — so that it applies whenever its
// premises hold — and every rule below is well-formed BY CONSTRUCTION:
// the obligation is met where the rule is written, not proved about
// the system afterwards. Some of these obligations are discharged by
// one genuine meta-theorem.
//
// THE INVERSION LEMMA (by mutual induction on derivations, all forms
// at once, assuming nothing of the rules' well-formedness — each rule
// is a case, and an ill-formed one would be a failing case): a
// derivable type of a former's shape has derivably
// well-formed components at that former's arities — if
// Γ ⊦ A → B type then Γ ⊦ A type and Γ ▷ A ⊦ B type, if
// Γ ⊦ (a₀ ≡ a₁ ∈ A) : Ω then Γ ⊦ a₀ : A and Γ ⊦ a₁ : A, and likewise
// for ×, ⊎, /, ∥·∥, the QIIT sorts and ν; if Γ ⊦ Rec l̄ Δ type then
// Γ ⊦ Δ tel, l̄ distinct and |l̄| = |Δ| — and, for an EQUATION with a
// former on either side, the same for that side (the two forms of the
// lemma are proved together). This is not evident: Γ ⊦ A → B type
// need not come from ty-pi — it may come from ty-coe along an
// equation that el-reflect read off a hypothesis, from ty-lift, or
// from a substitution equation — so the components are recovered by
// following every rule. PROOF SKETCH. The former rules pass their
// components through their premises. The delicate cases are the ones
// every extensional theory has: el-reflect, where the equation comes
// from an inhabitant s of a proposition and the parts are read off
// the proposition's own formation (which is part of the derivation of
// s's type, hence of Γ ctx when s is a hypothesis); the coercions
// el-ty-coe / el-eq-ty-coe / el-coe-ctx, where the target's
// well-formedness is the right-hand form of the lemma at the
// coercing equation; el-sym and el-trans, which swap and chain the
// two forms; the universe bridge and the prop lifts, which move
// between the levelled type judgement and the universes and need the
// tower's own rules (ty-univ, ty-prop) for the universe in the type
// slot; absurdity (el-zero-e at an equality prop), where the
// components are the prop's formation premises; and the
// theory-of-signatures zone, whose Nova pieces are read off the ToS
// derivation. No case consults the meaning of a term: the lemma is
// about derivations and holds in every model.
//
// WELL-FORMEDNESS, by construction: with inversion in hand, each rule's
// premises and their presuppositions give its conclusion's. This is
// what lets a rule omit a premise: el-pi-e
// concludes at B[id, e] from f : A → B and e : A alone because
// inversion of A → B type gives Γ ▷ A ⊦ B type; el-sigma-e₂ concludes
// at B[id, t .π₁] from t : A × B alone because inversion of A × B type
// gives B; el-reflect concludes a₀ ≐ a₁ : A from s : (a₀ ≡ a₁ ∈ A)
// alone because inversion of the proposition gives the sides at A; an
// injectivity rule hypothesises the equation of the composites alone,
// because it presupposes the composites and inversion gives their
// components. The premises kept although well-formedness would not
// need them are the handles of the CONGRUENCE convention. The setoid model
// validates the same entailments semantically — a true equation has a
// type for its type slot and sides that are members of it — which is
// the reading PRESUPPOSITIONS in the conventions describes.
//
// EVERY TYPE HAS A FINITE LEVEL (meta-theorem, by induction on the
// derivation of Γ ⊦ A type): no rule introduces a type at ω alone —
// every formation clause is stated at an arbitrary level ℓ, and ω
// enters only by ty-lift. So "no top" stays true, and any two types
// share a finite level: the equality proposition (A₀ ≡ A₁ ∈ 𝕌ℓ) of
// two types always exists.

// A derivable judgement under Γ ▷ A presupposes Γ ctx and Γ ⊦ A type,
// so a premise stated under Γ ▷ A carries A's well-formedness with it
// (and likewise for iterated extensions). Γ ▷ 𝕌ℓ is well-formed
// (𝕌ℓ type ℓ₊₁): a context may bind a variable ranging over the types
// of a level. What no context binds is "all types": there is no
// universe of all universes, no 𝕌ω, and Γ ⊦ 𝕌ℓ : 𝕌ℓ is not derivable
// (Girard) — a universe is typed one level up and nowhere below.

