# Types

// THE TOWER. The types are the terms Γ ⊦ A type ℓ, formed by the
// formation clause of each former (in the former's own section below)
// — one per former, stating its formation and its level in one rule,
// ℓ ∈ ℕ ∪ {ω} (LEVEL INDICES) — and related to the universes by the
// BRIDGE below. This section holds what is GENERIC to types: the
// universe former and the bridge, cumulativity, type equality,
// substitution, coercion, and the injectivity commitment.
//
//  * A CUMULATIVE TOWER 𝕌₀ : 𝕌₁ : 𝕌₂ : … — each universe a type one
//    level up, never at its own level (Girard), and each a
//    SUBUNIVERSE of the next: the types of level ℓ are the elements of
//    𝕌ℓ (univ-i, univ-e), and a type of level ℓ is one of every level
//    above (ty-lift). There is no top and no universe of all types;
//    "large" means "one level up", and the unbounded Γ ⊦ A type says
//    only that A is a type of SOME finite level (Judgements). Levels
//    are LITERALS: the theory has no level variables and no level
//    polymorphism, and a statement quantifying over 𝕌₀ is a type of
//    level 1.
//  * Ω BELOW THE BOTTOM: Ω : 𝕌₁ (ty-prop), and every proposition is a
//    type of level 0 (prop-lift). Ω itself is deliberately NOT a 𝕌₀ code —
//    the one asymmetry of the tower, and a semantic fact, not a
//    convention: in a realizability reading a proposition is a
//    subsingleton and hence data, while the type of all propositions
//    is not (a program cannot tell two propositions apart), so Ω : 𝕌₀
//    is refuted there and A → Ω stays one level above A. In the
//    setoid reading Ω is the two-point set and nothing would break;
//    the theory keeps the reading both models share.
//  * Every EXCLUSION is by absence of a derivation, not by grammar: a
//    universe at its own level, Ω at 𝕌₀, a Π over all types — each
//    would need a typing no rule gives.
//  * Type equality from absurdity needs NO rule, it is DERIVABLE:
//    from Γ ⊦ t : 𝟘, el-zero-e at the type (A ≡ B ∈ 𝕌ℓ), ℓ a common
//    level of A and B — code-eq admits the universes, see the Ω block —
//    gives 𝟘-elim t : (A ≡ B ∈ 𝕌ℓ), and el-reflect with univ-eq-e
//    concludes Γ ⊦ A ≐ B type. (The same derivation gives a ≐ b : C at ANY type
//    under absurdity — absurdity collapses every equation, type
//    equations included.)

Γ ctx
--------------- (ty-univ) // one level up, never at its own
Γ ⊦ 𝕌ℓ type ℓ₊₁

## Universes

// THE BRIDGE between the levelled type judgement and the universes:
// the types of level ℓ are EXACTLY the elements of 𝕌ℓ (univ-i,
// univ-e), and a type equation between two of them is exactly an
// equation at 𝕌ℓ (univ-eq-i, univ-eq-e). There is no decoding former:
// a code IS a type, and a type of finite level IS a code. univ-eq-i
// is MANDATORY, not optional: it is what keeps the equality props
// (A ≡ B ∈ 𝕌ℓ) and (A ≡ B ∈ 𝕌ℓ₊₁) equi-true at level-ℓ types (whence
// ≐-equal by code-prop-eq), so facts established one level up
// descend; and it is the only way INTO a universe equation from a
// type equation. CUMULATIVITY is ty-lift, the monotonicity of the
// level: a type of level ℓ is one of every level above, ω included.
// (The former code-lift, A ≐ B : 𝕌ℓ ⟹ A ≐ B : 𝕌ℓ₊₁, is univ-eq-e,
// ty-lift and univ-eq-i; the former code-restrict is univ-eq-i
// itself.) SEMANTICS: the codes of level ℓ are a sub-collection of
// those of level ℓ+1 (the setoid model's `el` embedding is an
// inclusion); the level is a property of the CODE, so equal codes
// have equal levels (ty-coe, below), and type equality restricted to
// a level is that level's own — exactly univ-eq-i. Cumulativity acts
// at the ROOT of a type only: a function into 𝕌ℓ is not thereby a
// function into 𝕌ℓ₊₁ (η-expand it); a context entry at 𝕌ℓ is not one
// at 𝕌ℓ₊₁.

Γ ⊦ A type ℓ
--------------- (univ-i)
Γ ⊦ A : 𝕌ℓ

Γ ⊦ A : 𝕌ℓ
--------------- (univ-e)
Γ ⊦ A type ℓ

Γ ⊦ A₀ ≐ A₁ type
Γ ⊦ A₀ type ℓ
Γ ⊦ A₁ type ℓ
-------------------- (univ-eq-i)
Γ ⊦ A₀ ≐ A₁ : 𝕌ℓ

Γ ⊦ A₀ ≐ A₁ : 𝕌ℓ
-------------------- (univ-eq-e)
Γ ⊦ A₀ ≐ A₁ type

Γ ⊦ A type ℓ
ℓ ≼ ℓ′
--------------- (ty-lift)   // cumulativity: ℓ′ any level above ℓ, ω included
Γ ⊦ A type ℓ′

## Type equality

// Γ ⊦ A₀ ≐ A₁ type is an EQUIVALENCE, level-free, presupposing that
// both sides are types; its congruences are the -cong rules of the
// type formers (CONGRUENCE, conventions), and the bridge above
// relates it to the universes' equations. ty-coe moves a level
// across it: the level is a property of the code (SEMANTICS above).

Γ ⊦ A type
------------------ (ty-refl)
Γ ⊦ A ≐ A type

Γ ⊦ A₀ ≐ A₁ type
------------------ (ty-sym)
Γ ⊦ A₁ ≐ A₀ type

Γ ⊦ A₀ ≐ A₁ type      Γ ⊦ A₁ ≐ A₂ type
---------------------------------------- (ty-trans) // via A₁
Γ ⊦ A₀ ≐ A₂ type

Γ ⊦ A₀ ≐ A₁ type
Γ ⊦ A₀ type ℓ
------------------ (ty-coe)
Γ ⊦ A₁ type ℓ

## Substitution

// A substitution moves no level: levels are literals. The action on
// each former's types is at the former (ty-sub-pi and its kin); the
// atoms are inert.

Γ₁ ⊦ A type ℓ
σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
--------------------- (ty-sub)   // ty-sub-cong: Γ₁ ⊦ A₀ ≐ A₁ type and
Γ₀ ⊦ A[σ] type ℓ                 //   σ₀ ≐ σ₁ give Γ₀ ⊦ A₀[σ₀] ≐ A₁[σ₁] type

Γ ⊦ A type
----------------------- (ty-sub-id) // ADM, as el-sub-id
Γ ⊦ A[id] ≐ A type

Γ₂ ⊦ A type
σ : Γ₁ ⇒ Γ₂
τ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
--------------------------------------- (ty-sub-comp) // ADM, as el-sub-comp
Γ₀ ⊦ A[σ ∘ τ] ≐ A[σ][τ] type

σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
------------------------------------------------------------------------- (ty-sub-atoms)
Γ₀ ⊦ 𝟘[σ] ≐ 𝟘 type
Γ₀ ⊦ 𝟙[σ] ≐ 𝟙 type
Γ₀ ⊦ ℕ[σ] ≐ ℕ type
Γ₀ ⊦ 𝕌ℓ[σ] ≐ 𝕌ℓ type
Γ₀ ⊦ Ω[σ] ≐ Ω type

