## Telescopes at a level

// Γ ⊦ Δ tel ℓ, ℓ ∈ ℕ ∪ {ω}, is the telescope judgement itself: tel
// is its ω instance, and the finite instances are what the record
// former is formed from (see "Record types"). META-LEMMAS, each
// entrywise by the corresponding type rule:
//   * (raise) Γ ⊦ Δ tel ℓ and ℓ ≼ ℓ′ give Γ ⊦ Δ tel ℓ′, by ty-lift.
//     The contexts of the later entries are unchanged: Γ ▷ A records
//     A, not its level.
//   * (existence) every Γ ⊦ Δ tel is one at some finite ℓ — a
//     telescope is finite and every type has a finite level; take the
//     greatest and raise.
//   * (congruence) Γ ⊦ Δ₀ ≐ Δ₁ tel and Γ ⊦ Δ₀ tel ℓ give Γ ⊦ Δ₁ tel ℓ,
//     by ty-coe entrywise (the right entry read over the left prefix
//     by coercion).
//   * (substitution, coercion) tel-sub, tel-coe-ctx and tel-eq-coe-ctx
//     hold at every level, as stated: levels are literals, a
//     substitution moves none.

