## Operations on spines

// A substitution extended by a spine, and the spine of a telescope's
// variables: the plumbing of the QIIT readings (Γ · Δ and ↑Δ are in
// Telescopes).

//   (⇛ is the ToS's Π, NOT Nova's →. The variable discipline is
//   NAMELESS, like Nova's own: ⬡ᵢ counts inductive binders and context
//   entries ONLY — ToS variables are ORTHOGONAL to Nova's ☐ᵢ, and the
//   two calculi never touch each other's variables. In examples, named
//   binders (x : A) ⇛ …, (𝕧 : El 𝕥) ⇛ … and named entries are DISPLAY
//   SUGAR for the indexed core. There is no inductive λ: terms of
//   inductive-Π type arise only as partial applications, which is all
//   signatures need.)
//
// Strict positivity and externality are GRAMMATICAL, by two features
// working together. First, Π domains are only Nova types or El-codes —
// U and Π-types never occur left of a ⇛. Second, the two Π's bind into
// DIFFERENT ZONES of the dual-zone judgements below: an external
// binder grows the NOVA zone Γ, an inductive binder the ToS zone Φ;
// Nova types are typed over Γ alone, so they cannot mention an
// inductive variable — sort-free automatically, with no projection and
// no side condition.
//
// Entry classification, by the END of the entry's type (𝔄ᵉ, Arity
// and end; every qiit-type ends in U or El, so the classification is
// exhaustive — there are no other entry forms to exclude):
//     … ⇛ U               a SORT (its Πs are the index arity)
//     … ⇛ El (𝕤 ī)        a POINT constructor into sort 𝕤
//     … ⇛ El (𝕝 ≡ 𝕣)      an EQUATION constructor (imposes 𝕝 ≐ 𝕣)
//
// THE READING ⟦·⟧ interprets checked ToS syntax as Nova syntax over
// the ALGEBRA CONTEXT Γ·⟦Φ⟧ — a signature as a telescope, its entries
// as the telescope's variables; the ToS system itself never reads.
//
σ : Γ ⇒ Ξ
Ξ ⊦ Δ tel
