# Ω: the propositions

Γ ctx
------------ (ty-prop) // and NOT Γ ⊦ Ω : 𝕌₀ — see THE TOWER
Γ ⊦ Ω type 1

// Ω is the universe of mere propositions, below the tower's bottom
// (Ω : 𝕌₁, THE TOWER); its equality discipline is the mirror image
// of the structural universes'. Structural codes are compared
// STRUCTURALLY (Injectivity, under Types); Ω's codes are compared by
// INHABITATION alone (code-prop-eq). Each discipline is sound only on
// its own cluster, and the two COEXIST at every 𝕌ℓ on disjoint
// clusters (PROP-CUMULATIVITY: a proposition is a 𝕌₀ code; Ω itself
// is a 𝕌₁ code and never a 𝕌₀ code; no rule crosses the clusters,
// and there is no Ω analogue of any inj rule).
//
// PROPOSITIONAL EQUALITY LIVES HERE: (a₀ ≡ a₁ ∈ A) is an ELEMENT of
// Ω, not a type (the OTT design — observational equality in a
// definitionally irrelevant Prop). What this buys, and what it
// forfeits:
//  * Proof irrelevance is inherited from el-prf-prop — no separate
//    η-rule at ≡ is needed, and equality hypotheses never carry data.
//  * The canonical proof is ⋆, and there is no other. This is forced, not
//    stylistic: code-prop-eq + prop-lift + el-ty-coe move proofs
//    between iff-equal props UNCHANGED (a true equation is ≐-equal to
//    ∥𝟙∥ at Ω), so every inhabited prop must have literally the same
//    canonical form.
//  * A is an ARBITRARY type, the universes included: equality props
//    exist between types, (A ≡ B ∈ 𝕌ℓ) : Ω — TYPE EQUALITY IS A
//    PROPOSITION, at every level, reflection-complete exactly like
//    element equality (el-eq-i, el-reflect at A = 𝕌ℓ).
//  * Ω-positions take equations directly — quotient relations need no
//    squash (ℕ × ℕ / (p q. p .π₁ + q .π₂ ≡ p .π₂ + q .π₁ ∈ ℕ)), and
//    the squashed-equality connective below is subsumed.
//  * NO injectivity, inherited from Ω's discipline; but a 𝕌₀-code,
//    by prop-lift, so equational content IS storable in a small type
//    directly — a Σ over a proposition, a positivity witness with its
//    modulus — with the extensional equality of the prop cluster
//    riding along (what the prf-code quotient trick below
//    manufactures, the lift gives directly).
//
// Notes:
//  * Realizer irrelevance is FORCED, not chosen: code-prop-eq +
//    prop-lift + el-ty-coe move an element between iff-equal props
//    UNCHANGED, which is sound only if those props (as types) have
//    literally the same canonical forms. So a prop never exposes the
//    squashed proofs: its one canonical form is ⋆ (cf. NuPRL's Ax),
//    and el-prf-prop equates all members. Consequently ∥A∥, as a
//    type, does NOT reduce to A, and ∥−∥ is NOT injective:
//    ∥𝟙∥ ≐ (Z ≡ Z ∈ ℕ) : Ω holds by code-prop-eq while the squashees
//    are structurally distinct. Ω adds no computation rules beyond
//    substitution actions (squash's idempotence is ADMISSIBLE, not a
//    computation rule — see code-squash-idem); the preface's normalization story is
//    unchanged.
//  * Squash is the only way in: ∥-∥ takes an arbitrary TYPE, not a
//    𝕌-code, so the connectives are signature definitions, not rules —
//      ⊤ ≔ ∥𝟙∥,  ⊥ ≔ ∥𝟘∥,  p ∧ q ≔ ∥p × q[↑]∥,
//      p ⊃ q ≔ ∥p → q[↑]∥,  ∀ over A ≔ ∥A → p∥,
//      ∃ over A ≔ ∥A × p∥
//    (props stand directly in the domains and components — prop-lift)
//    — equality (≡) is the one PRIMITIVE prop beside ∥-∥ (squashing
//    it again is redundant by code-squash-idem). Every other definable
//    prop is ∥-∥-headed, so the eliminators below lose no generality;
//    derived intro/elim principles come from el-squash-i /
//    el-squash-e-* over the underlying former.
//  * Elimination goes only into equations and props: a squashed
//    hypothesis may be unsquashed exactly when the goal cannot
//    observe WHICH proof was used — equational goals (judgements do
//    not consult witnesses) and propositional goals (the witness is
//    ⋆ either way). With ≡ Ω-valued, el-squash-e-eq is ADMISSIBLE:
//    equality props exist at every type (large included), so el-eq-i
//    under the binder, el-squash-e-prf and el-reflect derive it. It
//    is kept as a rule for the kernel's convenience. There is
//    deliberately NO eliminator into arbitrary types — el-prf-prop
//    would force it constant, and it would refute witness
//    irrelevance in the model.
//  * IMPREDICATIVITY. ∥-∥ squashes arbitrary types of every level,
//    including quantifications over Ω itself and over any 𝕌ℓ. This is sound
//    because the candidate denotations of props form a FIXED
//    two-point lattice — the empty and the unit subsingleton setoid —
//    that does not grow with the quantification domain: a universally
//    quantified prop is an infimum in that lattice, witnessed
//    uniformly by ⋆ (precedent: the proof-irrelevant setoid models,
//    where Prop is exactly this lattice; the PER models of CC ran the
//    same argument with realizers). The
//    restrictions above are the license for this; each blocks a known
//    paradox:
//      - proof irrelevance blocks Girard/Hurkens: nothing can be
//        stored in a prop and retrieved for diagonalization (in
//        particular, Church encodings through Ω are sterile — no
//        data can be smuggled past the size restrictions);
//      - no elimination into arbitrary types blocks unique choice /
//        description, and with it the quotient+choice collapses
//        (Chicli–Pottier–Simpson);
//      - no 𝕌₀-code for Ω ITSELF blocks Reynolds/Cantor: A → Ω is
//        one level above A, so no type contains its own powerset.
//        Individual propositions ARE 𝕌₀ codes (prop-lift), and that
//        is harmless — it holds up to iff without the lift:
//        with Id the QIIT identity family over a small carrier
//        (Id : (x y : a) ⇛ U ; refl : (x : a) ⇛ El (Id x x)), take
//        prf r ≔ Id (ℕ / r̂) (class Z) (class (S Z)), a 𝕌₀-code whose
//        decoding is inhabited iff r — el-quot-eq plus el-qiit-intro
//        one way, effectivity along (x ≡ y ∈ ℕ) ∨ r plus qiit
//        elimination the other. So the load-bearing prohibition was
//        never on propositions, only on their universe: propositions
//        and powersets embed into the codes of some 𝕌ℓ, never into
//        the elements of a small type — quotient elements cannot
//        store a proposition (coherence forces eliminators out of
//        𝟙/r̂-style types constant), and a universe is never at its
//        own level. Equality props have 𝕌₀ codes like every
//        proposition; what they store is ⋆.
//    Payoff: least relations by intersection — e.g. an equivalence
//    closure r⁺ of an arbitrary relation r, defined by quantifying
//    over all Ω-valued relations containing r — with no inductive
//    machinery. And since ty-quot takes its relation at Ω rather
//    than at a universe, A / r⁺ is at the level of A: quotients by
//    generated congruences stay small.
//  * Consequences for quotients (whose relation slot is Ω-valued —
//    see ty-quot):
//      1. Mutually implied relations give EQUAL quotient types:
//         code-prop-eq under Γ ▷ A ▷ A[↑] gives R₀ ≐ R₁ : Ω, then
//         ty-quot; dually ty-quot-inj returns only iff-content.
//         A proof-relevant presentation is recovered as A / ∥R∥.
//      2. Effectivity, in the ONLY form it can take: quotient equality
//         is the equivalence CLOSURE. For R : Ω over Γ ▷ A ▷ A[↑] with
//         no assumption whatever,
//
//           class a ≐ class b : A / R  ⟺  R⁺[id, a, b] inhabited
//
//         (⟸) R⁺ is least among the equivalences containing R, and
//         (class ☐₁ ≡ class ☐₀ ∈ A / R) is one — el-quot-eq for
//         containment, the EQUIVALENCE RULES for the rest.
//         (⟹) quot-elim at the constant motive Ω with f ≔ R⁺[id, a, ☐₀]:
//         coherence is R⁺ a x ⟺ R⁺ a y under R[id, x, y], by
//         code-prop-eq from R⁺'s OWN transitivity and symmetry (this is
//         why the motive is the closure and not R: nothing about R is
//         needed); then el-quot-beta at class a, congruence along the
//         class equation, prop-lift and el-ty-coe carry R⁺'s
//         reflexivity proof to b. Both directions stay inside A / R — no
//         transport to A / R⁺, which by item 1 is a DIFFERENT type.
//         Corollary: where R is an equivalence, R⁺ collapses into it by
//         leastness and effectivity holds ON THE NOSE — the familiar
//         form, with the hypotheses that make it true.
//         The naive form — R itself back, pointwise, for arbitrary R —
//         is REFUTABLE, not merely unproved: ≐ is an equivalence at
//         every judgement class while ty-quot's relation slot is
//         arbitrary, so at R ≔ (S ☐₁ ≡ ☐₀ ∈ ℕ) one has
//         class Z ≐ class (S (S Z)) by transitivity, whence a proof
//         of (S Z ≡ S (S Z) ∈ ℕ), whence Z ≐ S Z by el-reflect and
//         S-injectivity, whence 𝟘. Nothing may read R off a class
//         equation; only R⁺.
//      3. Equality proofs reflect directly: el-reflect reads
//         a₀ ≐ a₁ : B off any s : (a₀ ≡ a₁ ∈ B) — no squash
//         apparatus is involved.
//  * SEMANTICS. In the setoid model a prop, read as a type through
//    prop-lift, denotes a subsingleton setoid: carrier 𝟙 if p is
//    true, 𝟘 otherwise (all elements related either way) — where ∥A∥ is true iff ⟦A⟧'s carrier is
//    inhabited, and (a₀ ≡ a₁ ∈ A) is true iff ⟦a₀⟧ ~ ⟦a₁⟧ in ⟦A⟧'s
//    relation; ∥A∥ ~ ∥B∥ : Ω iff A and B are equi-inhabited.
//    THE ∈-𝕌ℓ INSTANCE: (A ≡ B ∈ 𝕌ℓ) is true iff ⟦A⟧ and ⟦B⟧ are
//    EQUAL CODES — the model's type equality at level ℓ (a MIXED PER:
//    structural on the code summand, iff on the prop summand — see
//    PROP-CUMULATIVITY), which is exactly
//    what el-reflect at 𝕌ℓ reads back. It is sound by the same
//    two-layer construction: prop-truth is defined against the full
//    type system anyway, and code equality of every level is
//    available at that stage; this prop's type of proofs is the
//    same subsingleton as every other, so nothing is storable through
//    it (no Hurkens vector), and Ω itself has no 𝕌₀ code — the
//    firewall clauses of the impredicativity note are untouched.
//    code-prop-eq holds on the nose (iff-equal props have IDENTICAL
//    denotations); el-squash-e-* are validated by instantiating their
//    premise at any carrier element — the conclusion never consults
//    which one. Model note: the prop layer cannot be built by the
//    same stagewise induction as the rest of the type system (the
//    Π-over-Ω clause consults Ω's full domain, non-monotonically); it
//    is instead given IN ADVANCE — the fixed lattice above, with
//    prop-truth defined against the full type system. A two-layer
//    construction, as in the impredicative-Prop setoid models (and,
//    before them, the PER models of CC). The Ω-valued quotient slot
//    adds no further impredicative dependency: the quotient clause
//    consumes Ω-truth POINTWISE (⟦A / R⟧ keeps ⟦A⟧'s carrier
//    and coarsens its relation by the truth of R at each pair — in
//    the setoid model a quotient is FREE), so quotient codes stay
//    small however impredicative their relation — propositional
//    resizing, in HoTT terms, which the setoid model validates.
//    PRECISELY: the coarsened relation must still be an EQUIVALENCE
//    (that is what a setoid is), so it is the equivalence closure of
//    ⟦A⟧'s relation together with R's truth — exactly R⁺'s
//    denotation. "Coarsens by the truth of R at each pair" is the
//    closure's description only when R is already an equivalence
//    containing ≐_A; in general read the closure, and effectivity
//    (item 2 above) is the syntactic counterpart. This does NOT
//    collapse A / R into A / R⁺: type equality is equality of CODES,
//    the quotient code carries its relation, and R, R⁺ are not
//    pointwise equi-inhabited — so ty-quot-inj is untouched, at the
//    price that two quotient types may denote the same setoid while
//    remaining distinct types.

Γ ⊦ A type
------------------ (code-squash)
Γ ⊦ ∥A∥ : Ω

Γ ⊦ A type
Γ ⊦ a : A
Γ ⊦ b : A
---------------------- (code-eq) // A an ARBITRARY type, the universes
Γ ⊦ (a ≡ b ∈ A) : Ω              //   included: type equality is a
                                 //   proposition. A is a premise so that
                                 //   code-eq-cong doubles it

Γ ⊦ p : Ω
---------------------------- (code-squash-idem) // squash is idempotent on
Γ ⊦ ∥p∥ ≐ p : Ω                                 //   props. ADMISSIBLE, by
                                                //   code-prop-eq: ∥p∥ and p
                                                //   are equi-inhabited —
                                                //   el-squash-i one way,
                                                //   el-squash-e-prf the
                                                //   other. NOT a β: the
                                                //   redex is not
                                                //   syntax-directed (its
                                                //   side condition is a
                                                //   typing), so this is
                                                //   an equation and not a
                                                //   contraction

Γ ▷ p ⊦ s : q[↑]
Γ ▷ q ⊦ t : p[↑]
----------------------------- (code-prop-eq) // propositional extensionality:
Γ ⊦ p ≐ q : Ω                                //   mutually implied props are
                                             //   equal codes (the binders
                                             //   extend by the props
                                             //   directly — prop-lift)

Γ ⊦ t : A
--------------------- (el-squash-i)
Γ ⊦ ⋆ : ∥A∥

Γ ⊦ a₀ ≐ a₁ : A
------------------------------ (el-eq-i) // INTERNALIZATION — PRIMITIVE:
Γ ⊦ ⋆ : (a₀ ≡ a₁ ∈ A)                    //   the judgement gives the
                                         //   proposition its canonical
                                         //   inhabitant

Γ ⊦ s : (a₀ ≡ a₁ ∈ A)
-------------------------- (el-reflect) // REFLECTION — PRIMITIVE: any
Γ ⊦ a₀ ≐ a₁ : A                         //   inhabitant of the
                                        //   proposition gives the
                                        //   judgement. The two rules
                                        //   make the proposition an
                                        //   internalization of the
                                        //   judgement, not its
                                        //   definition. ⋆-CANONICITY
                                        //   is then ADMISSIBLE: from s,
                                        //   code-prop-eq at p and ∥𝟙∥
                                        //   (s[↑] one way, el-squash-i
                                        //   with ()[↑] the other) gives
                                        //   p ≐ ∥𝟙∥ : Ω, and
                                        //   prop-lift with el-ty-coe
                                        //   carries el-squash-i's
                                        //   ⋆ : ∥𝟙∥ into p — any
                                        //   inhabited prop admits ⋆;
                                        //   the ⋆'s occurring in TERMS
                                        //   sit at reflexive equations
                                        //   and come from el-eq-i at a
                                        //   diagonal

Γ ⊦ p : Ω
Γ ⊦ t₀ : p
Γ ⊦ t₁ : p
----------------------- (el-prf-prop) // proof irrelevance: elements of
Γ ⊦ t₀ ≐ t₁ : p                       //   a PROPOSITION are equal;
                                      //   propositionhood is the
                                      //   premise p : Ω

Γ ⊦ s : ∥A∥
Γ ▷ A ⊦ b₀[↑] ≐ b₁[↑] : B[↑]
------------------------------ (el-squash-e-eq)
Γ ⊦ b₀ ≐ b₁ : B

Γ ⊦ q : Ω
Γ ⊦ s : ∥A∥
Γ ▷ A ⊦ t : q[↑]
------------------------ (el-squash-e-prf)
Γ ⊦ ⋆ : q

## Prop-cumulativity

// There is no proof-type former: a proposition IS
// its type of proofs, by the lift below — a type of level 0, the
// bottom of the tower, whence of every level by ty-lift — and its
// equality lifts (prop-lift-eq) and restricts (prop-restrict).
// prop-restrict is MANDATORY for the same reason univ-eq-i is (it
// keeps the props (p ≡ q ∈ Ω) and (p ≡ q ∈ 𝕌₀) equi-true at props, so
// the ∈-slot stays well-defined). THE ASYMMETRY with the universe
// bridge, stated plainly: univ-eq-e imports nothing (a level's
// equality is the restriction of type equality on the nose), but
// prop-lift-eq imports PROPOSITIONAL EXTENSIONALITY into type
// equality at level 0 — on the prop cluster, type equality is mere
// equivalence (code-prop-eq).
// Type equality at EVERY universe is thereafter MIXED: structural on
// the code cluster, extensional on the prop cluster. This is no cost
// of the lift: with the quotient slot Ω-valued, the 𝕌₀-code
// prf r ≔ Id (ℕ / r̂) (class Z) (class (S Z)) carries every
// proposition into 𝕌₀ up to iff (see the impredicativity note in the
// Ω block), and prf r ≐ prf r′ : 𝕌₀ whenever r ⟺ r′ — the small
// universe's equality is mixed without the lift, which only makes it
// so directly. prop-lift-eq is PRIMITIVE, not an el-sub-cong
// instance (the master congruence at ☐₀ over Γ ▷ Ω concludes at Ω,
// not at type — nothing else lifts the coarse equality). CROSS-CLUSTER equations
// are underivable by absence: ∥𝟙∥ ≐ 𝟙 type has no derivation —
// prop-restrict needs both sides at Ω (𝟙 is not: Ω's only formers
// are ≡ and ∥·∥), and no structural rule reaches a prop-headed side
// — and the model refutes them (disjoint summands, see SEMANTICS
// below). Both are contractible; the theory keeps them intensionally
// distinct, exactly as A / R vs A / R⁺. SEMANTICS: each universe's
// codes gain a PROP summand, disjoint from the structural codes,
// whose constructor argument is QUOTIENTED by iff — the PER of 𝕌ℓ is
// constructor-structural on one summand and extensional on the
// other; no-confusion BETWEEN the summands is the meta-property that
// refutes cross-cluster equalities. Ω ITSELF has
// no 𝕌₀ code (THE TOWER): the lift is of propositions, never of
// their universe.

Γ ⊦ p : Ω
---------------- (prop-lift)
Γ ⊦ p type 0

Γ ⊦ p₀ ≐ p₁ : Ω
-------------------- (prop-lift-eq)
Γ ⊦ p₀ ≐ p₁ type

Γ ⊦ p₀ : Ω
Γ ⊦ p₁ : Ω
Γ ⊦ p₀ ≐ p₁ type
-------------------- (prop-restrict)
Γ ⊦ p₀ ≐ p₁ : Ω

## Substitution action

Γ₁ ⊦ A type
σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
------------------------------------ (el-sub-squash)
Γ₀ ⊦ ∥A∥[σ] ≐ ∥A[σ]∥ : Ω

Γ₁ ⊦ a₀ : A
Γ₁ ⊦ a₁ : A
σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
----------------------------------------------------- (el-sub-eq)
Γ₀ ⊦ (a₀ ≡ a₁ ∈ A)[σ] ≐ (a₀[σ] ≡ a₁[σ] ∈ A[σ]) : Ω

Γ₁ ⊦ p : Ω
Γ₁ ⊦ ⋆ : p
σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
--------------------------------- (el-sub-star)
Γ₀ ⊦ ⋆[σ] ≐ ⋆ : p[σ]

# Record types (labelled telescopes)

// Rec l̄ Δ is a telescope Δ with a label per entry. The labels are a
// parallel list — Δ stays an ordinary nameless telescope, so a label
// never binds and the tel-/sp- machinery is reused as is.

// SIDE CONDITIONS on label lists — meta-level, context-free.

· distinct

l̄ distinct
l ∉ l̄
------------
l l̄ distinct

// |l̄| = |Δ|: the lists have the same length

## Fields

// Γ ⊦ t / l̄ ↪ Δ: the fields l̄ of t have the types Δ — a SUFFIX of t's
// record, over Γ, the earlier fields instantiated at t's projections.
// A projection and the spine of projections t.l̄ are typed by it.

Γ ⊦ t : Rec l̄ Δ
---------------- (rec-fields)
Γ ⊦ t / l̄ ↪ Δ

Γ ⊦ t / l l̄ ↪ A ◁ Δ
----------------------- (rec-fields-step)
Γ ⊦ t / l̄ ↪ Δ[id, t.l]

Γ ⊦ t₀ ≐ t₁ : Rec l̄′ Δ′      Γ ⊦ Δ₀ ≐ Δ₁ tel      Γ ⊦ t₀ / l̄ ↪ Δ₀
----------------------------------------------------------------- (rec-fields-coe)
Γ ⊦ t₁ / l̄ ↪ Δ₁

Γ ⊦ t / l̄ ↪ Δ
--------------- (sp-rec-proj)
Γ ⊦ t.l̄ : Δ

Γ ⊦ t / · ↪ ε
----------------- (sp-rec-proj-empty)
Γ ⊦ t.· ≐ · : ε

Γ ⊦ t / l l̄ ↪ A ◁ Δ
--------------------------------- (sp-rec-proj-ext)
Γ ⊦ t.(l l̄) ≐ t.l, t.l̄ : A ◁ Δ

## Rules

// Γ ⊦ ē : Δ gives Γ ⊦ Δ tel ℓ at some ℓ (existence); Γ ⊦ t : Rec l̄ Δ
// gives Δ at a level, l̄ distinct and |l̄| = |Δ| by inversion.

Γ ⊦ Δ tel ℓ
l̄ distinct
|l̄| = |Δ|
------------------ (ty-rec)
Γ ⊦ Rec l̄ Δ type ℓ

Γ ⊦ ē : Δ
l̄ distinct
|l̄| = |Δ|
----------------------- (el-rec-i)
Γ ⊦ ⟨l̄ ↪ ē⟩ : Rec l̄ Δ

Γ ⊦ t / l l̄ ↪ A ◁ Δ
-------------------- (el-rec-e)   // congruence: at t₀, then rec-fields-coe
Γ ⊦ t.l : A

// Computation: by the position of the label. The premises are
// el-rec-i's — the components typed, as in el-sigma-beta₁/₂ — not the
// typing of the record: that a typed record has typed components is no
// lemma of the theory, and the rule must not assert it. The miss step
// is well-typed by induction along l̄: the fields of the two records
// agree at the earlier labels by this rule.

Γ ⊦ e, ē : A ◁ Δ
l l̄ distinct
|l l̄| = |A ◁ Δ|
---------------------------- (el-rec-beta)
Γ ⊦ ⟨l l̄ ↪ e, ē⟩.l ≐ e : A

Γ ⊦ e, ē : A ◁ Δ
l′ l̄ distinct
|l′ l̄| = |A ◁ Δ|
Γ ⊦ ⟨l̄ ↪ ē⟩.l : B
--------------------------------------- (el-rec-beta-miss)
Γ ⊦ ⟨l′ l̄ ↪ e, ē⟩.l ≐ ⟨l̄ ↪ ē⟩.l : B

// Uniqueness, in el-sigma-eta's form and orientation. At l̄ = · this is
// ⟨⟩ ≐ t : Rec · ε — the empty record is a unit type.

Γ ⊦ t : Rec l̄ Δ
---------------------------- (el-rec-eta)
Γ ⊦ ⟨l̄ ↪ t.l̄⟩ ≐ t : Rec l̄ Δ

// Injectivity, at ONE label list: labels are syntax and compare
// syntactically. That records with different label lists are different
// types is no-confusion — like Π against Σ, not a rule, and a
// meta-property of consistent contexts only.

Γ ⊦ Rec l̄ Δ₀ ≐ Rec l̄ Δ₁ type
------------------------------ (ty-rec-inj)
Γ ⊦ Δ₀ ≐ Δ₁ tel

// Substitution action.

Γ₁ ⊦ Δ tel
l̄ distinct
|l̄| = |Δ|
σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
------------------------------------ (ty-sub-rec)
Γ₀ ⊦ (Rec l̄ Δ)[σ] ≐ Rec l̄ Δ[σ] type

Γ₁ ⊦ ē : Δ
l̄ distinct
|l̄| = |Δ|
σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
------------------------------------------- (el-sub-record)
Γ₀ ⊦ ⟨l̄ ↪ ē⟩[σ] ≐ ⟨l̄ ↪ ē[σ]⟩ : Rec l̄ Δ[σ]

Γ₁ ⊦ t.l : A
σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
------------------------------- (el-sub-rec-proj)
Γ₀ ⊦ (t.l)[σ] ≐ t[σ].l : A[σ]

# Quotient inductive-inductive types (signatures)
//
// These are the inductive-inductive quotient types of
// Altenkirch–Kaposi. A reference x[σ] to a signature defined once in
// Σ (sig-qctx) is the practical form: the signature is checked once,
// its formers are compared by name and spine (IDENTITY below), and a
// parametrised family — lists over A — has a place for its parameter.
// The scheme SUBSUMES ℕ, (⊎) and (/), and covers indexed inductive
// types (well-founded trees included) and quotient inductive types
// generally; ℕ, (⊎) and (/) are retained for now.
//
// THE EXTENSIONAL PAYOFF. Under equality reflection (with Ω for
// proof-irrelevance) every type is a set: no higher paths, no coherence
// tower, no transport. A path constructor is therefore an equation
// IMPOSED judgementally (via el-reflect), and the eliminator's path
// premises collapse to WELL-DEFINEDNESS conditions — precisely
// quot-elim's f⁼ premise, one per equation, with no apd/transport.
// This degeneration is what lets the scheme be POSTULATED precisely
// rather than through a tower of coherences (contrast the intensional
// HIIT signatures, which need the full apparatus).

## Theory of signatures

// Grammar. The ToS is a SMALL DEPENDENT TYPE
// THEORY of its own: qiit-contexts are built out of qiit-types,
// qiit-terms are typed at qiit-types, and all argument passing is by
// the ToS's own Π/λ/application — there is no spine syntax. A
// SIGNATURE is nothing but a closed qiit-context: sorts, point
// constructors and equation constructors are ordinary entries,
// distinguished by the HEAD of their type alone.

// INSTANTIATION is not a bespoke operation — both binder
// instantiations are calculus instances:
//   EXTERNAL, by a Nova term t: the NOVA substitution [id, t] acting
//     through ToS syntax (Nova substitution below);
//   INDUCTIVE, by a ToS term 𝕥: the ToS substitution [𝕚𝕕, 𝕥]
//     (Substitution below).
// The two calculi act on disjoint namespaces, so their actions commute.

## Theory-of-signatures well-formedness

// The dual zone Γ ; Φ: Γ is the NOVA zone (the ambient context plus
// all external binders in scope), Φ the ToS zone (declared entries
// plus inductive binders). A signature WRITTEN OUT is a closed
// qiit-context — during checking, the growing context Φ IS the
// signature-so-far, so a later declaration reaches earlier sorts and
// constructors by qtm-var, with no prefix or ambient-𝒮 device.

### Judgements

Γ ctx
-------------- (qctx-empty)
Γ ⊦ ε qctx ℓ

Γ ⊦ Φ qctx ℓ      Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝔄 qty ℓ
---------------------------------- (qctx-ext)   // qctx-ext-cong: the equation
Γ ⊦ Φ ▷ 𝔄 qctx ℓ                                //   of signatures BY CONTENT (IDENTITY)

(Γ ⊦ x ≔ 𝒮 qctx ℓ) ∈ Σ
σ : Θ ⇒ Γ norm      ℓ ≼ ℓ′
--------------------------- (qctx-ref)   // qctx-ref-cong: the equation BY NAME,
Σ Θ ⊦ x[σ] qctx ℓ′                       //   on the substitutions alone

(Γ ⊦ x ≔ 𝒮 qctx ℓ) ∈ Σ
σ : Θ ⇒ Γ norm
------------------------ (qctx-ref-unfold)
Σ Θ ⊦ x[σ] ≐ 𝒮[σ] qctx

// PREFIX: Φ is 𝒮 up to some entry, with i entries after it — the
// POSITION of the entry Φ ends at, as ⬡ᵢ names it in 𝒮; a reference
// by its content.

Γ ⊦ Φ qctx
Γ ⊦ 𝒮 qctx
----------- (qctx-prefix)
Γ ⊦ Φ ⊑ᵢ 𝒮

Γ ⊦ Φ qctx
------------ (qctx-prefix-refl)
Γ ⊦ Φ ⊑₀ Φ

Γ ⊦ Φ ▷ 𝔄 ⊑ᵢ 𝒮
---------------- (qctx-prefix-contract)
Γ ⊦ Φ ⊑ᵢ₊₁ 𝒮

Γ ⊦ Φ₀ ≐ Φ₁ qctx      Γ ⊦ 𝒮₀ ≐ 𝒮₁ qctx      Γ ⊦ Φ₀ ⊑ᵢ 𝒮₀
-------------------------------------------------------- (qctx-prefix-coe)
Γ ⊦ Φ₁ ⊑ᵢ 𝒮₁

// SMALL EXTENSION: Φ′ is Φ followed by El entries only — the local
// binders of a zone (Elimination).

Γ ⊦ Φ qctx
Γ ⊦ Φ′ qctx
------------ (qctx-small)
Γ ⊦ Φ ⊑ₛ Φ′

Γ ⊦ Φ qctx
----------- (qctx-small-refl)
Γ ⊦ Φ ⊑ₛ Φ

Γ ⊦ Φ ⊑ₛ Φ′      Γ ; Φ′ ⊦ 𝕥 : U
-------------------------------- (qctx-small-ext)
Γ ⊦ Φ ⊑ₛ Φ′ ▷ El 𝕥

Γ ⊦ Φ₀ ≐ Φ₁ qctx      Γ ⊦ Φ′₀ ≐ Φ′₁ qctx      Γ ⊦ Φ₀ ⊑ₛ Φ′₀
----------------------------------------------------------- (qctx-small-coe)
Γ ⊦ Φ₁ ⊑ₛ Φ′₁

Γ ⊦ Φ ⊑ᵢ 𝒮
------------------ (qctx-remainder)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝒮 ∖ Φ qtel

Γ ⊦ 𝒮 qctx
----------------------- (qctx-remainder-refl)
Γ ; 𝒮 ⊦ 𝒮 ∖ 𝒮 ≐ ε qtel

Γ ⊦ Φ ▷ 𝔄 ⊑ᵢ 𝒮
------------------------------------ (qctx-remainder-contract)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝒮 ∖ Φ ≐ 𝔄 ◁ 𝒮 ∖ (Φ ▷ 𝔄) qtel

Γ ⊦ Φ₀ ≐ Φ₁ qctx      Γ ⊦ 𝒮₀ ≐ 𝒮₁ qctx      Γ ⊦ Φ₀ ⊑ᵢ 𝒮₀
-------------------------------------------------------- (qctx-remainder-coe)
Γ ; Φ₁ ⊦ 𝒮₁ ∖ Φ₁ ≐ 𝒮₀ ∖ Φ₀ qtel

Γ ⊦ Φ ⊑ᵢ 𝒮
------------------------ (qctx-remainder-lemma) // ADM
Γ ⊦ Φ · (𝒮 ∖ Φ) ≐ 𝒮 qctx

Γ ⊦ Φ qctx ℓ
----------------- (qty-univ)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ U qty ℓ

Γ ⊦ Φ qctx ℓ      Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 : U
------------------------------- (qty-el)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ El 𝕥 qty ℓ

Γ ⊦ A type ℓ      Γ ▷ A ; Φ[↑] ⊦ 𝔄 qty ℓ
----------------------------------------- (qty-pi-ext)   // binds a NOVA variable:
Γ ; Φ ⊦ A ⇛ 𝔄 qty ℓ                                      //   the Nova zone grows

Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 : U      Γ ; Φ ▷ El 𝕥 ⊦ 𝔄 qty ℓ
------------------------------------------ (qty-pi-ind)   // binds a ToS variable:
Γ ; Φ ⊦ El 𝕥 ⇛ 𝔄 qty ℓ                                    //   the ToS zone grows

// LOOKUP Φ‖ᵢ, the type ⬡ᵢ names in Φ: as Γ‖ₙ, with the ToS shift.

Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝔄 qty
--------------------------------- (qty-lookup-zero)
Γ ; Φ ▷ 𝔄 ⊦ (Φ ▷ 𝔄)‖₀ ≐ 𝔄[⇑] qty

Γ ; Φ ⊦ Φ‖ᵢ qty      Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝔄 qty
-------------------------------------------- (qty-lookup-suc)
Γ ; Φ ▷ 𝔄 ⊦ (Φ ▷ 𝔄)‖ᵢ₊₁ ≐ (Φ‖ᵢ)[⇑] qty

Γ ; Φ ⊦ Φ‖ᵢ qty
------------------ (qtm-var)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ ⬡ᵢ : Φ‖ᵢ

Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 : A ⇛ 𝔄      Γ ⊦ t : A
---------------------------------- (qtm-app-ext)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 t : 𝔄[id, t]

Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 : El 𝕦 ⇛ 𝔄      Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥' : El 𝕦
---------------------------------------------- (qtm-app-ind)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 𝕥' : 𝔄[𝕚𝕕, 𝕥']

Γ ▷ A ; Φ[↑] ⊦ 𝕥 : 𝔄
------------------------ (qtm-lam-ext)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ λ 𝕥 : A ⇛ 𝔄

Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥₀ : El 𝕦      Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥₁ : El 𝕦
------------------------------------------ (qtm-eq)     // equation code in U
Γ ; Φ ⊦ (𝕥₀ ≡ 𝕥₁) : U

### Levels

// The level index ℓ of qctx ℓ, qty ℓ and qtel ℓ ranges over ℕ ∪ {ω}
// (LEVEL INDICES, conventions): every Nova type embedded is typed at
// level ℓ at its position, and qctx, qty, qtel are the ω instances.
// Raising the level is admissible, entrywise by ty-lift. The level is
// LOAD-BEARING: with an external domain one level up — say
// (a : 𝕌ℓ) — the sort's decoding would contain 𝕌ℓ as a RETRACT
// (eliminate at constant motive 𝕌ℓ with method a ↦ a), the classic
// type-in-type collapse; so such a signature is at ℓ+1 and its sorts
// are types of level ℓ+1, and the model agrees — a universe cannot be
// constructed while consulting its own totality.

### Substitution

// The ToS substitution calculus, mirroring Nova's (𝕚𝕕/⇑/∘/ext; the
// lift is derived). ς₀ ≐ ς₁ : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁ is EXTENSIONAL, as σ₀ ≐ σ₁
// (qsub-extensional, qsub-empty-unique): the other equations of the
// calculus are admissible, as at Substitutions.

Γ ⊦ Φ qctx
------------------- (qsub-id)
Γ ⊦ 𝕚𝕕 : Φ ⇒ Φ

Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝔄 qty
---------------------- (qsub-wk)
Γ ⊦ ⇑ : Φ ▷ 𝔄 ⇒ Φ

Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁      Γ ⊦ τ : Φ₁ ⇒ Φ₂
-------------------------------------- (qsub-comp)
Γ ⊦ τ ∘ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₂

Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁      Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ 𝕥 : 𝔄[ς]
---------------------------------------- (qsub-ext)
Γ ⊦ (ς, 𝕥) : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁ ▷ 𝔄

Γ ⊦ ς₀ : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁ ▷ 𝔄      Γ ⊦ ς₁ : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁ ▷ 𝔄
Γ ⊦ ⇑ ∘ ς₀ ≐ ⇑ ∘ ς₁ : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁      Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ ⬡₀[ς₀] ≐ ⬡₀[ς₁] : 𝔄[⇑ ∘ ς₁]
------------------------------------------------------------------------ (qsub-extensional)
Γ ⊦ ς₀ ≐ ς₁ : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁ ▷ 𝔄

Γ ⊦ ς₀ : Φ ⇒ ε      Γ ⊦ ς₁ : Φ ⇒ ε
------------------------------------ (qsub-empty-unique)
Γ ⊦ ς₀ ≐ ς₁ : Φ ⇒ ε

Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁      Γ ; Φ₁ ⊦ 𝔄 qty
--------------------------------------------- (qsub-lift)   // ADM
Γ ⊦ ς ▷ 𝔄 ≐ (ς ∘ ⇑, ⬡₀) : Φ₀ ▷ 𝔄[ς] ⇒ Φ₁ ▷ 𝔄

Γ ; Φ₁ ⊦ 𝔄 qty      Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁
------------------------------------- (qty-sub)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ 𝔄[ς] qty

Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁
----------------------- (qty-sub-univ)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ U[ς] ≐ U qty

Γ ; Φ₁ ⊦ 𝕥 : U      Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁
------------------------------------- (qty-sub-el)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ (El 𝕥)[ς] ≐ El 𝕥[ς] qty

Γ ⊦ A type      Γ ▷ A ; Φ₁[↑] ⊦ 𝔄 qty      Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁
------------------------------------------------------------ (qty-sub-pi-ext)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ (A ⇛ 𝔄)[ς] ≐ A ⇛ 𝔄[ς[↑]] qty

Γ ; Φ₁ ⊦ 𝕥 : U      Γ ; Φ₁ ▷ El 𝕥 ⊦ 𝔄 qty      Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁
-------------------------------------------------------------- (qty-sub-pi-ind)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ (El 𝕥 ⇛ 𝔄)[ς] ≐ El 𝕥[ς] ⇛ 𝔄[ς ▷ El 𝕥] qty

Γ ; Φ₁ ⊦ Ψ qtel      Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁
------------------------------------- (qtel-sub)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ Ψ[ς] qtel

Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁
------------------------ (qtel-sub-empty)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ ε[ς] ≐ ε qtel

Γ ; Φ₁ ⊦ 𝔄 qty      Γ ; Φ₁ ▷ 𝔄 ⊦ Ψ qtel      Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁
------------------------------------------------------------ (qtel-sub-ext)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ (𝔄 ◁ Ψ)[ς] ≐ 𝔄[ς] ◁ Ψ[ς ▷ 𝔄] qtel

Γ ; Φ₁ ⊦ 𝔗 qdual      Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁
-------------------------------------- (qdual-sub)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ 𝔗[ς] qdual

Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁
------------------------- (qdual-sub-empty)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ ε[ς] ≐ ε qdual

Γ ⊦ A type      Γ ▷ A ; Φ₁[↑] ⊦ 𝔗 qdual      Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁
------------------------------------------------------------- (qdual-sub-ext)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ (A ◁ 𝔗)[ς] ≐ A ◁ 𝔗[ς[↑]] qdual

Γ ; Φ₁ ⊦ 𝕥 : U      Γ ; Φ₁ ▷ El 𝕥 ⊦ 𝔗 qdual      Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁
---------------------------------------------------------------- (qdual-sub-ind)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ (El 𝕥 ◁ 𝔗)[ς] ≐ El 𝕥[ς] ◁ 𝔗[ς ▷ El 𝕥] qdual

Γ ; Φ₁ ⊦ 𝕥 : 𝔄      Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁
------------------------------------- (qtm-sub)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ 𝕥[ς] : 𝔄[ς]

Γ ; Φ ⊦ Φ‖ᵢ qty
--------------------------- (qtm-sub-var-id)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ ⬡ᵢ[𝕚𝕕] ≐ ⬡ᵢ : Φ‖ᵢ

Γ ; Φ ⊦ Φ‖ᵢ qty      Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝔄 qty
--------------------------------------- (qtm-sub-var-wk)
Γ ; Φ ▷ 𝔄 ⊦ ⬡ᵢ[⇑] ≐ ⬡ᵢ₊₁ : (Φ‖ᵢ)[⇑]

Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁      Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ 𝕥 : 𝔄[ς]
---------------------------------------- (qtm-sub-var-hit)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ ⬡₀[ς, 𝕥] ≐ 𝕥 : 𝔄[ς]

Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁      Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ 𝕥 : 𝔄[ς]      Γ ; Φ₁ ⊦ ⬡ᵢ : 𝔅
----------------------------------------------------------- (qtm-sub-var-miss)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ ⬡ᵢ₊₁[ς, 𝕥] ≐ ⬡ᵢ[ς] : 𝔅[ς]

Γ ; Φ₂ ⊦ ⬡ᵢ : 𝔄      Γ ⊦ τ : Φ₁ ⇒ Φ₂      Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁
---------------------------------------------------------- (qtm-sub-var-comp)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ ⬡ᵢ[τ ∘ ς] ≐ ⬡ᵢ[τ][ς] : 𝔄[τ][ς]

Γ ; Φ₁ ⊦ 𝕥 : A ⇛ 𝔄      Γ ⊦ t : A      Γ ⊦ ς : Φ₀ ⇒ Φ₁
------------------------------------------------------- (qtm-sub-app-ext)
Γ ; Φ₀ ⊦ (𝕥 t)[ς] ≐ 𝕥[ς] t : 𝔄[id, t][ς]

