## Signatures

// What the formers carry. A signature is a closed
// qiit-context WRITTEN OUT, or a REFERENCE x[σ] to a signature entry
// of Σ, instantiated at its parameters by a normal substitution — the
// shape a term reference has (el-sig-var).

// The FORMERS keep 𝒮 as written: the initial algebra of a reference is
// built from formers AT the reference (ι below), so the types of a
// named QIIT mention its name and never its entries.
//
// Unfolding (qctx-ref-unfold) commutes with substitution at a
// reference (qctx-nsub-ref), a raw identity.

### Initial algebra

// The spine of the formers at 𝒮, entry by entry: each entry is the
// λ over its arity instantiated at the entries before it, of the
// former at its position (a sort, a point constructor, or ⋆ for an
// equation entry, whose end is a proposition imposed by
// el-qiit-path). The formers carry 𝒮 AS WRITTEN — a reference stays a
// reference — so the induction is on a PREFIX Φ ▷ 𝔄 ⊑ᵢ 𝒮 of 𝒮's
// content with the whole 𝒮 a parameter: ι_𝒮(Φ) is the algebra of the
// prefix, and i the POSITION of the entry, the former's index. Still
// to be formalised: ty-qiit, el-qiit-* at the prefix algebra ι_𝒮(Φ) in
// place of ι(𝒮), which breaks the circle between the outer rules and
// ι's typing; and the equation ⟦𝔄⟧ ≐ Π ⟦𝔄⟧ᵗ. ⟦𝔄⟧ᵉ (induction on 𝔄,
// by refl-end-pi-ext's substitution), which types the entries. That
// ι(𝒮) is a spine is then a META-LEMMA by the outer rules, by
// induction along 𝒮.

Γ ⊦ 𝒮 qctx
------------------------- (ini)
Γ ⊦ ι(𝒮) ≐ ι_𝒮(𝒮) : ⟦𝒮⟧

Γ ⊦ Φ ⊑ᵢ 𝒮
---------------------------------------- (ini-prefix)
Γ ⊦ ι_𝒮(Φ) : ⟦Φ⟧

Γ ⊦ 𝒮 qctx
---------------------- (ini-empty)
Γ ⊦ ι_𝒮(ε) ≐ · : ε

Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝔄 qty      Γ ⊦ Φ ▷ 𝔄 ⊑ᵢ 𝒮
Γ · 𝔄ᵗᴺ ; Φ[↑𝔄ᵗᴺ] · 𝔄ᵗᵀ ⊦ 𝔄ᵉ ≐ U qty
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ (ini-sort)
Γ ⊦ ι_𝒮(Φ ▷ 𝔄) ≐ ι_𝒮(Φ), λ ⟦𝔄⟧ᵗ[id, ι_𝒮(Φ)]. 𝒮.i ☐(⟦𝔄⟧ᵗ[id, ι_𝒮(Φ)]) : ⟦Φ⟧ ▷ ⟦𝔄⟧

Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝔄 qty      Γ ⊦ Φ ▷ 𝔄 ⊑ᵢ 𝒮
Γ · 𝔄ᵗᴺ ; Φ[↑𝔄ᵗᴺ] · 𝔄ᵗᵀ ⊦ 𝔄ᵉ ≐ El (⬡ⱼ ī) qty      // ⬡ⱼ a sort, by its type
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ (ini-point)
Γ ⊦ ι_𝒮(Φ ▷ 𝔄) ≐ ι_𝒮(Φ), λ ⟦𝔄⟧ᵗ[id, ι_𝒮(Φ)]. 𝒮.i ☐(⟦𝔄⟧ᵗ[id, ι_𝒮(Φ)]) : ⟦Φ⟧ ▷ ⟦𝔄⟧

Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝔄 qty      Γ ⊦ Φ ▷ 𝔄 ⊑ᵢ 𝒮
Γ · 𝔄ᵗᴺ ; Φ[↑𝔄ᵗᴺ] · 𝔄ᵗᵀ ⊦ 𝕝 : El 𝕦
Γ · 𝔄ᵗᴺ ; Φ[↑𝔄ᵗᴺ] · 𝔄ᵗᵀ ⊦ 𝕣 : El 𝕦
Γ · 𝔄ᵗᴺ ; Φ[↑𝔄ᵗᴺ] · 𝔄ᵗᵀ ⊦ 𝔄ᵉ ≐ El (𝕝 ≡ 𝕣) qty
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ (ini-eq)
Γ ⊦ ι_𝒮(Φ ▷ 𝔄) ≐ ι_𝒮(Φ), λ ⟦𝔄⟧ᵗ[id, ι_𝒮(Φ)]. ⋆ : ⟦Φ⟧ ▷ ⟦𝔄⟧

## Identity

// (structural, with a pathway by name). 𝒮.𝕤 ē carries the
// signature 𝒮; two QIIT types are equal exactly when their signatures,
// sorts (positions), and indices are — homogeneous with every other
// former. Signatures have an EQUATION of their own,
// Γ ⊦ 𝒮₀ ≐ 𝒮₁ qctx — a judgement of its own, like the context and
// telescope equations, Γ ⊦ 𝒮 qctx its unary form —
// reached by TWO PATHWAYS:

// The equation of qiit-contexts, Γ ⊦ Φ₀ ≐ Φ₁ qctx, is the
// COMPONENTWISE comparison: both well-formed, entry by entry the SAME
// indexed ToS syntax, and their embedded Nova pieces equal (≐) — a
// domain at its universe, an argument at its domain, each over the
// right-hand side's binders. The ToS structure is compared
// INTENSIONALLY, and the NAMELESS discipline makes that comparison
// PLAIN STRUCTURAL EQUALITY of indexed syntax — there are no names, so
// there is no α to quotient by; like universe codes. It is spelled
// per former by the CONGRUENCE convention — qctx-ext-cong,
// qty-el-cong, qty-pi-ext-cong, qty-pi-ind-cong, qtm-app-ext-cong,
// qtm-app-ind-cong, qtm-lam-ext-cong, qtm-eq-cong, with qtm-var and
// qty-univ refl instances — and no rule beyond these. The
// inductive-inductive self-reference is a BOUND reference (a ⬡-index)
// inside the finite signature, so the comparison is finite and
// iso-recursive — it never unfolds the fixpoint into its carrier, and
// needs no equirecursive/coinductive machinery. (Signature equality is
// finer than initial-algebra isomorphism — it distinguishes entry
// reorderings — but SOUND; choosing a syntactic granularity over the
// semantic one is the commitment Injectivity, under Types already
// makes: models collapsing structurally-distinct types are excluded.)
//
// THE TWO PATHWAYS. By-name (qctx-ref-cong) is ADMISSIBLE from
// by-content — the unfoldings 𝒮[σ₀] and 𝒮[σ₁] (qctx-ref-unfold) are
// equal piece by piece, by el-sub-cong — so the relation is
// by-content's, an equivalence. By-name is stated because it decides
// the common case —
// two uses of ONE name — on the syntax, without evaluating either
// side: the rigid-rigid-before-unfolding discipline, as a rule.
// By-content is what makes a name TRANSPARENT: a named QIIT equals the
// QIIT written out with the same entries, two entries with the same
// content name the same types, and an alias (Γ ⊦ x ≔ y[σ] qctx ℓ) is
// an abbreviation. It is the pathway to take when the names differ.
//
// META-LEMMA. Equal signatures have equal entries, arities and
// readings, positionwise — by content this is the comparison itself
// (a reading is a recursion on the syntax compared), by name it is
// tel-sub on the entry's arity — and their initial algebras are
// equal spines, by the formers' own congruence along the signature.
// This is what types the LEFT instance of a former's -cong rule at
// the RIGHT instance's arity.
//
// A NAME for a QIIT is therefore its Σ-entry: the signature is
// checked once, and every sort, constructor and eliminator of it is a
// former at x[σ]. Consequently the
// theory is UNIFORMLY structural, QIITs included, so (/) is a genuine
// instance — A / R is 𝒮.𝕢 · for
//     𝒮 = ( 𝕢 : U ; cls : (x : A) ⇛ El 𝕢 ;
//           eq : (x y : A) ⇛ (h : R[x,y]) ⇛ El (cls x ≡ cls y) )
// — and the primitive (/) is kept for convenience, not necessity.

## Formation

// Every QIIT former is SATURATED — spine-applied, like S t, class a
// and every other Nova former. The ToS is curried internally;
// currying stops at the Nova boundary.
Γ ⊦ 𝒮 qctx ℓ
Γ · (𝒮‖𝕤)ᵗᴺ ; 𝒮[↑(𝒮‖𝕤)ᵗᴺ] · (𝒮‖𝕤)ᵗᵀ ⊦ (𝒮‖𝕤)ᵉ ≐ U qty
Γ ⊦ ē : ⟦𝒮‖𝕤⟧ᵗ[id, ι(𝒮)]
------------------------------------------------ (ty-qiit)   // ty-qiit-cong: Γ ⊦ 𝒮₀ ≐ 𝒮₁ qctx and
Γ ⊦ 𝒮.𝕤 ē type ℓ                                             //   ē₀ ≐ ē₁ at 𝒮₁'s arity (IDENTITY)

## Introduction

// Point constructor, FULLY SATURATED: θ supplies every
// argument at once, and 𝒮.𝕔 θ is the canonical form of its sort. A
// bare curried 𝒮.𝕔 : ⟦𝔄⟧[id, ι(𝒮)] is deliberately NOT a term: in the empty
// context it would be a non-λ inhabitant of a Π-type, breaking
// canonicity at Π (a closed Π-inhabitant is a λ — a meta-property of
// definitional signatures, by the usual gluing argument) — the same
// violation the judgemental el-qiit-path avoids at ≡-types. Nothing is
// lost: a partial application is a λ away, λ (𝒮.𝕔 (…, ☐₀)).

Γ ⊦ 𝒮 qctx
Γ ⊦ θ : ⟦𝒮‖𝕔⟧ᵗ[id, ι(𝒮)]
Γ · (𝒮‖𝕔)ᵗᴺ ; 𝒮[↑(𝒮‖𝕔)ᵗᴺ] · (𝒮‖𝕔)ᵗᵀ ⊦ (𝒮‖𝕔)ᵉ ≐ El (⬡ⱼ ī) qty
------------------------------------------------------------- (el-qiit-intro)
Γ ⊦ 𝒮.𝕔 θ : ⟦⬡ⱼ ī⟧[(id, θᴺ, ι(𝒮), θᵀ)]

## Path

// Equation constructor: the equation HOLDS, as a JUDGEMENT —
// el-quot-eq's shape, generalized. Deliberately no proof term is
// minted: equality is Ω-valued, so an equation entry's read type is a
// PROP, whose one canonical form is ⋆ — a constructor form there would
// be a second canonical inhabitant, refuting witness irrelevance.
// Nothing is lost — the prop is inhabited by ⋆ via el-eq-i once
// el-qiit-path imposes the equation (which is what ι's equation
// entries are) — and any witness data the equation is conditional on
// (e.g. the quotient's R) is simply a binder of 𝔄, instantiated inside
// θ.

Γ · (𝒮‖𝕔)ᵗᴺ ; 𝒮[↑(𝒮‖𝕔)ᵗᴺ] · (𝒮‖𝕔)ᵗᵀ ⊦ 𝕝 : El 𝕦
Γ · (𝒮‖𝕔)ᵗᴺ ; 𝒮[↑(𝒮‖𝕔)ᵗᴺ] · (𝒮‖𝕔)ᵗᵀ ⊦ 𝕣 : El 𝕦
Γ · (𝒮‖𝕔)ᵗᴺ ; 𝒮[↑(𝒮‖𝕔)ᵗᴺ] · (𝒮‖𝕔)ᵗᵀ ⊦ (𝒮‖𝕔)ᵉ ≐ El (𝕝 ≡ 𝕣) qty
Γ ⊦ θ : ⟦𝒮‖𝕔⟧ᵗ[id, ι(𝒮)]
------------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-qiit-path)
Γ ⊦ ⟦𝕝⟧[id, θᴺ, ι(𝒮), θᵀ] ≐ ⟦𝕣⟧[id, θᴺ, ι(𝒮), θᵀ] : ⟦𝕦⟧[id, θᴺ, ι(𝒮), θᵀ]

## Congruence and injectivity

// Injectivity: type equality is STRUCTURAL, so equal saturated
// sort types at ONE signature have equal spines — the ty-pi-inj block,
// extended to the QIIT former.

Γ ⊦ 𝒮.𝕤 ē₀ ≐ 𝒮.𝕤 ē₁ type
-------------------------------------------------------- (ty-qiit-inj)
Γ ⊦ ē₀ ≐ ē₁ : ⟦𝒮‖𝕤⟧ᵗ[id, ι(𝒮)]

## Elimination

// THE DISPLAYED READING _ᴰ. The eliminator's data — one MOTIVE per
// sort, one METHOD per point constructor, one COHERENCE per equation
// constructor — is one spine d̄ of the DISPLAYED telescope ⟦𝒮⟧ᴰ 𝒰̄,
// read over the algebra context and instantiated at the initial
// algebra. The reading is taken at a ZONE: a prefix Φ ⊑ 𝒮 and a
// qiit-context Φ′ with Φ ⊑ₛ Φ′, the inductive binders opened past it.
// (That _ᴰ commutes with Nova substitution and ToS weakening through
// ToS syntax, ⟦Φ[σ] ⊑ Φ′[σ]⟧ᴰ = ⟦Φ ⊑ Φ′⟧ᴰ[σ · ⟦𝒮⟧], (⟦𝔄⟧ᴰ 𝒰 t)[σ′] =
// ⟦𝔄[σ]⟧ᴰ 𝒰 t[σ′] for σ′ the lift of σ to the zone, and _ᴰ of a ToS
// weakening is _ᴰ weakened, are raw identities, as at the reading.)
//
// TARGETS: one slot per entry of 𝒮 — for a sort the universe its
// motive lands in, _ for a point or equation entry; a motive into Ω
// is NOT one into 𝕌₀ (THE TOWER), it is the target an induction into
// a proposition names, where every coherence holds by el-prf-prop.

Γ ⊦ 𝒮 qctx
------------------- (targets-qctx)
Γ ⊦ 𝒰̄ targets 𝒮

Γ ; 𝒮 ⊦ 𝔄 qty
------------------- (targets-qty)
Γ ; 𝒮 ⊦ 𝒰 targets 𝔄

Γ ; 𝒮 ⊦ 𝔄 qty
Γ · 𝔄ᵗᴺ ; 𝒮[↑𝔄ᵗᴺ] · 𝔄ᵗᵀ ⊦ 𝔄ᵉ ≐ U qty
Γ ⊦ 𝒰 type
---------------------------------------- (targets-qty-sort)
Γ ; 𝒮 ⊦ 𝒰 targets 𝔄

Γ ; 𝒮 ⊦ 𝔄 qty
Γ · 𝔄ᵗᴺ ; 𝒮[↑𝔄ᵗᴺ] · 𝔄ᵗᵀ ⊦ 𝔄ᵉ ≐ El 𝕥 qty
------------------------------------------- (targets-qty-el)
Γ ; 𝒮 ⊦ _ targets 𝔄

Γ ctx
----------------- (targets-qctx-empty)
Γ ⊦ · targets ε

Γ ⊦ 𝒰̄ targets Φ
Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝒰 targets 𝔄
------------------------ (targets-qctx-ext)
Γ ⊦ 𝒰̄, 𝒰 targets Φ ▷ 𝔄

// LOOKUP 𝒰̄‖ᵢ — the target at position i, as ⬡ᵢ names it.

Γ ⊦ 𝒰̄, 𝒰 targets Φ ▷ 𝔄
----------------------- (targets-lookup-zero)
(𝒰̄, 𝒰)‖₀ = 𝒰

Γ ⊦ 𝒰̄, 𝒰′ targets Φ ▷ 𝔄      𝒰̄‖ᵢ = 𝒰
------------------------------------- (targets-lookup-suc)
(𝒰̄, 𝒰′)‖ᵢ₊₁ = 𝒰

